@startuml
skinparam style strictuml
title Domain Sequence Diagram - Study Plan Calculation

actor Student
participant "ScheduleController" as SC
participant "DegreeProgramService" as DPS
participant "ScheduleService" as SS
participant "StudyModuleService" as SMS
participant "Schedule" as S
participant "Semester" as Sem

Student -> SC : calculateSchedule(degreeProgramId)
activate SC

SC -> DPS : findById(degreeProgramId)
activate DPS
DPS --> SC : degreeProgram
deactivate DPS

SC -> SS : calculate(degreeProgram)
activate SS

SS -> SMS : findAllByDegreeProgramId(degreeProgramId)
activate SMS
SMS --> SS : modules
deactivate SMS

SS -> S : new Schedule()
activate S
S --> SS : schedule
deactivate S

note over SS
  Topological sort — Kahn's layered BFS:
  1. Build moduleMap (key → StudyModule) for O(1) lookup
  2. Build inDegree (key → count of unmet in-program prerequisites)
  3. Build dependents (key → list of modules that declare it as a prerequisite)
  4. Seed ready queue with all keys whose inDegree == 0
  5. Each iteration: snapshot the queue as a layer → create a new Semester →
     place every module in the layer → decrement inDegree of each dependent →
     enqueue dependents whose inDegree reaches 0 (for the next semester)
  6. After BFS drains: if placed < total, throw CyclicDependencyException
end note

alt no cyclic dependency
    loop for each topological layer (semester)
        SS -> Sem : new Semester(semesterNumber)
        activate Sem
        Sem --> SS : semester
        deactivate Sem
        SS -> S : addSemester(semester)
    end
    SS --> SC : schedule
else cyclic dependency detected
    SS --> SC : throws CyclicDependencyException
end

deactivate SS

alt schedule calculated successfully
    SC --> Student : redirect to schedule view\n(flash: successMessage + schedule)
else cyclic dependency
    SC --> Student : redirect to schedule view\n(flash: errorMessage)
end

deactivate SC
@enduml
